          },
          "description": {
            "value": "<p>You have a longer torso and broader shoulders than most hobgoblins, making your legs seem short by comparison. This gives you a strong, muscular core and lowers your center of gravity—features that assist you in riding and climbing—and you've trained at riding in a saddle from an extremely early age. You gain the @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.feats-srd.Item.Ride] feat. Additionally, you are not @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.Off-Guard] while you Climb.</p>"
          },
          "publication": {
            "license": "ORC",
            "remaster": true,
            "title": "Pathfinder Player Core 2"
          },
          "rules": [
            {
              "key": "GrantItem",
